# 4. Kubernetes Architecture

# Control Plane (Master Node)

Controls the entire Kubernetes cluster.

## Components

### API Server
Main entry point for Kubernetes commands.

### Scheduler
Decides which worker node will run the pod.

### Controller Manager
Monitors cluster state and maintains desired state.

### ETCD
Stores cluster configuration and data.

---

# Worker Node

Runs actual applications.

## Components

### Kubelet
Communicates with control plane.

### Kube Proxy
Handles networking.

### Container Runtime
Runs containers.

Examples:

- Docker
- containerd

---

# 5. Important Kubernetes Objects

## Pod
Smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes.

Usually contains one container.

## Deployment
Manages pods and replicas.

## ReplicaSet
Ensures required number of pods are running.

## Service
Exposes applications to users.

## Namespace
Used to separate environments and resources.

## ConfigMap
Stores configuration data.

## Secret
Stores sensitive information like passwords.

## Ingress
Manages external HTTP/HTTPS access.

